/*
:name: split_vs_packed_state
:type: lec
*/
// PYROPE-vs-PYROPE group (README "Pyrope ↔ Pyrope variants"): this file is the
// REFERENCE, and every `split_vs_packed_state_<N>.prp` beside it is LEC'd
// against it.
//
// THE CLAIM: SPLIT state and PACKED state are the same design, and `lhd lec`
// must prove it WITHOUT depending on being able to pair the two spellings by
// name. This side declares one register per lane; the variant declares one
// packed register and addresses lanes by bit range.
//
// Why this is its own fixture: pass/semdiff is a structural SHORTCUT that pairs
// state elements before the solver runs. Two flops named `e0`/`e1` have no
// counterpart in a single flop named `packed`, so semdiff cannot pair them and
// must decline -- that is FINE, and it is the whole point. Declining means the
// obligation goes to the solver, which must still return PROVEN.
//
// This used to be papered over: packed-array SROA stamped six `sroa_*`
// provenance attributes on every split leaf so semdiff could re-aggregate them
// back into one logical register. That collapse gave every leaf the SAME
// compare-point key and `collect_cuts` kept only the first, so N-1 of N
// obligations were silently DROPPED -- a lane-swap bug LEC'd as "PROVEN
// (structurally identical, no solver call)". The attributes are gone; this
// fixture is what says the honest path still works.
//
// MEASURED on this pair (2026-08-20), which is the invariant in one line:
//   lhd pass semdiff --stats  ->  state ref/impl 2/1, name-paired 0,
//                                 unpaired ref 2 impl 1, "DIFFERENCES present"
//   lhd lec                   ->  PROVEN equivalent
// semdiff declining is not a failure. Only lec returning anything other than
// PROVEN is.
//
// Deliberately tiny (2 lanes x 2 bits) so the solver call is cheap.
pub mod top(we:u1, d0:u2, d1:u2, sel:u1) -> (q:u2@[0]) {
  reg e0:u2 = 0
  reg e1:u2 = 0
  q = if sel != 0 { e1 } else { e0 }
  if we != 0 {
    e0 = d0
    e1 = d1
  }
}
